  {
   "evidence": "Lines 424-433: after `rw [..., \u2190 e.map_unitNormSubmodule]` the two directions use only `e.carrierEquiv_map_integralForm` and `apply_symm_apply`. The closest existing lemma, `TauCeti.BilinForm.IsIsometry.map_orthogonal` (LinearAlgebra/BilinearForm/Isometry.lean:158), is for a map from a form to itself (`f : M \u2192\u2097 M`), not for an `IntegralLattice.Isometry L M`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/PosDef/UnitNormSplitting.lean",
   "fix": "Add `Isometry.map_orthogonal (e : Isometry L M) (S : Submodule \u2124 L) : (L.integralForm.orthogonal S).map (e.carrierEquiv : L \u2192\u2097[\u2124] M) = M.integralForm.orthogonal (S.map e.carrierEquiv)`. Derive the unit-norm case from it via `e.map_unitNormSubmodule` and use it in `Isometry.unitNormComplement` (line 436).",
   "issue": "`Isometry.map_orthogonal_unitNormSubmodule` proves the general fact that an integral-lattice isometry carries `S^\u22a5` onto `(e S)^\u22a5` only for `S = unitNormSubmodule`. Its proof uses nothing about norm-one vectors once it rewrites with `\u2190 e.map_unitNormSubmodule`.",
   "line": 421
  }
 ],
